# Space: O(1) (no extra data structures; printing doesn’t count as stored space)

# 2) check_if_lists_have_an_equal(list_a, list_b)

# Time (worst case): O(a · b)
# (nested loops, compares every pair if no match)

# Time (best case): O(1)
# (if the first pair compared matches and returns immediately)

# Space: O(1)

# 3) print_10_or_less_elements(list_to_print)

# The loop runs min(len(list_to_print), 10) times.

# Time: O(1) (constant time, at most 10 prints)

# Space: O(1)

# 4) generate_list_trios(list_a, list_b, list_c)

